{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewNeural",
  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "02",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p02-visual-walkthrough-v3",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "fa2fb6631e8dfcdf9cf8298bf410798fd7e02940574231aaee90f66632ce389b",
        "2": "b76fa4ebe908a457039fc517de375ff8998286494d4dabb6867b3a9a8e8717de",
        "3": "5ad47ef903437df96949a1402e0336cbfa9fcb4d72f5c2aa4561f27568f078b4"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s01-c1-8a29429cfc23",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Learn to choose a private S three route without confusing it with access permission. An access point gives an application a named entry point and its own policy. The underlying bucket must still support the access.",
          "text_sha256": "8a29429cfc2338b7df09690b145f846f7daa216466359d3819dcb3f705ca1eb3",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ff7b74f2d1a3b57702b9844f1ba095c86914e415260e0c93e54e0314e8a16b48",
          "asset_sha256": "fa2fb6631e8dfcdf9cf8298bf410798fd7e02940574231aaee90f66632ce389b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s01-c2-22e54e198b5a",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For supported S three traffic from the V P C application, a gateway endpoint adds the route-table path. The route does not grant permission to read the bucket.",
          "text_sha256": "22e54e198b5a867ac750963a0f886085a737512d1bf469dea68f46ef40eb1377",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c17f3bf33362c744f04730a8eaf4801c5402001ede3b9abc1b7f403257ef5065",
          "asset_sha256": "fa2fb6631e8dfcdf9cf8298bf410798fd7e02940574231aaee90f66632ce389b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s01-c3-631009e183a4",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "An interface endpoint instead uses PrivateLink network interfaces. Choose that model when it fits the connectivity requirement, and budget for it. It does not replace the S three permissions check.",
          "text_sha256": "631009e183a46453d02b4d98b349380b4a814f0ce9eea076e702039f90c19c82",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2f1e5e1474afeb42584cee70b9e25d94f56662068ac20fad71c86143cc81998b",
          "asset_sha256": "fa2fb6631e8dfcdf9cf8298bf410798fd7e02940574231aaee90f66632ce389b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s01-c4-aeb43cf3ca8a",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "After the request reaches S three, it still faces the permissions check shown here. If a client can reach the service but gets Access Denied, inspect those policies before changing the network route.",
          "text_sha256": "aeb43cf3ca8acf0f0a1126843d8492b99af6c5f0e9e3c27dc17c77d90f20efca",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fbcb7464c86d1b78b046c7cd7d5602caf467e5f6ac268894ab1b4c569534e088",
          "asset_sha256": "fa2fb6631e8dfcdf9cf8298bf410798fd7e02940574231aaee90f66632ce389b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s02-c1-9bf916cc732f",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "S S E S three protects the stored bytes with S three-managed keys. If the design needs a customer-managed key policy or key-level control, consider S S E K M S.",
          "text_sha256": "9bf916cc732f67b61387743c494cc918d78ad2f8dcc6cc978f8f6dedb79a5741",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4a9c1bccaaee79aa2357e4552937444e40f0b8c799e9383354b0155ec8dc221a",
          "asset_sha256": "b76fa4ebe908a457039fc517de375ff8998286494d4dabb6867b3a9a8e8717de"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s02-c2-9e21492492a4",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "With S S E K M S, GetObject permission alone may not be enough. The reader must also be authorized to decrypt with the key, including when a replication or recovery workflow reads the data.",
          "text_sha256": "9e21492492a414f72d8c21d7b3928dd2e1eaba7f58a0a9b041558ae9671007c1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "68ef37a2fe96e6750c407a78827fb485af13bad1d1d561046a581e2b43ad46f8",
          "asset_sha256": "b76fa4ebe908a457039fc517de375ff8998286494d4dabb6867b3a9a8e8717de"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s02-c3-4437900b3642",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "H T T P S protects the request in transit. Neither key option replaces it. If the bucket must reject insecure requests, enforce H T T P S separately in a bucket policy.",
          "text_sha256": "4437900b364283f3fc0cef4c3a72ed290936838801d555f88367aeed4dc3b0c2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a84787083535d2d91c7b4dd6ff9c31616ff150a7085efd6ee90d810d690da93f",
          "asset_sha256": "b76fa4ebe908a457039fc517de375ff8998286494d4dabb6867b3a9a8e8717de"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s02-c4-d9fbb9f326ae",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The dashed key path represents an additional authorization check for S S E K M S. It is not another hop that the client uses to send the H T T P S request.",
          "text_sha256": "d9fbb9f326ae12f0ee8a981784341e284188346eef31cdf5f1f21782752ee61d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fd3fb0b188cd97a2ff554f42bc87f49131a29aad4740e3704cad6ef3ec4152fb",
          "asset_sha256": "b76fa4ebe908a457039fc517de375ff8998286494d4dabb6867b3a9a8e8717de"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s03-c1-2d6abf3c295f",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Uploading report dot C S V creates version one for that key.",
          "text_sha256": "2d6abf3c295f78479af8332c7389ffdd3b8e9fb27440192cdec83aa6f2303deb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "2d6abf3c295f78479af8332c7389ffdd3b8e9fb27440192cdec83aa6f2303deb",
          "asset_sha256": "5ad47ef903437df96949a1402e0336cbfa9fcb4d72f5c2aa4561f27568f078b4"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s03-c2-4b1fce20423a",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "An overwrite creates version two under the same key. Version one stays available instead of being destroyed.",
          "text_sha256": "4b1fce20423ae817e9a6acd4828318f7ab620005d265511d0c6bac5d781493a4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4b1fce20423ae817e9a6acd4828318f7ab620005d265511d0c6bac5d781493a4",
          "asset_sha256": "5ad47ef903437df96949a1402e0336cbfa9fcb4d72f5c2aa4561f27568f078b4"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s03-c3-f67e7a370e33",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "A simple delete without a version I D makes a delete marker current. A normal read now appears missing, but the saved versions remain.",
          "text_sha256": "f67e7a370e33f115460652703fb9e9376bda5b248d4c1ee5fb33cbe0b024e9f3",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "3078c7a4c37a4e113c4fd3b60181b12c57889f6b7534f8b25160c9c8afee6114",
          "asset_sha256": "5ad47ef903437df96949a1402e0336cbfa9fcb4d72f5c2aa4561f27568f078b4"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s03-c4-be69b5027c9e",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Remove the current marker to reveal the latest underlying version, or request the specific saved version you need.",
          "text_sha256": "be69b5027c9e3f3f01d20659f00f9b8a0add0ff564141b517a368d63ca3a1d0f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "be69b5027c9e3f3f01d20659f00f9b8a0add0ff564141b517a368d63ca3a1d0f",
          "asset_sha256": "5ad47ef903437df96949a1402e0336cbfa9fcb4d72f5c2aa4561f27568f078b4"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p02-redo-s03-c5-a1871825b5ca",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Deleting a version by I D removes that exact version permanently, not the other versions.",
          "text_sha256": "a1871825b5ca3fd7cda1b12033fc70ca91f689729f3fd43ba0fd3a955fc03018",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "531191dbeddfeb8be309981bbe14cb3caab58f804b563b87a55b1ee41418c07f",
          "asset_sha256": "5ad47ef903437df96949a1402e0336cbfa9fcb4d72f5c2aa4561f27568f078b4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "03",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p03-visual-walkthrough-v3",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "e1476bfb6197005033465cb2918b58c4eef024c336fcfcd11d9982fefdae8b53",
        "2": "fbd9545d625ce048173ca4301793d32009cfe8418ac1d43e827c81bfe993f27e",
        "3": "d35c7ca12252eafabbc3d5d8438395209881d5c9141b5572356db9c64df45796"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s01-c1-fec920822394",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Learn which control keeps an object version from being removed. Governance retention blocks ordinary deletion; bypass requires appropriate permission and an explicit bypass request. It is not the same as unrestricted administrator deletion.",
          "text_sha256": "fec920822394eb5f5972ca7de1ea16e9a078c98b8496d3e1b540ab390a3865d8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fec920822394eb5f5972ca7de1ea16e9a078c98b8496d3e1b540ab390a3865d8",
          "asset_sha256": "e1476bfb6197005033465cb2918b58c4eef024c336fcfcd11d9982fefdae8b53"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s01-c2-91f3b8c3e409",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Compliance retention protects the version until the date expires. Even the account root user cannot delete that protected version or shorten its retention while it applies.",
          "text_sha256": "91f3b8c3e409c97dffc967d50e1b55cc862c4743edd3716190f190e3df7f094c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "91f3b8c3e409c97dffc967d50e1b55cc862c4743edd3716190f190e3df7f094c",
          "asset_sha256": "e1476bfb6197005033465cb2918b58c4eef024c336fcfcd11d9982fefdae8b53"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s01-c3-5b70d21ee439",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Legal hold is separate and has no automatic expiry. An authorized principal can remove it. Apply retention or a hold to the object version that actually needs protection, and decide the recovery implications first.",
          "text_sha256": "5b70d21ee43913091065b6d1a9b9ebc76fb6e452ee251cfca162b2f8a7fc03b6",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5b70d21ee43913091065b6d1a9b9ebc76fb6e452ee251cfca162b2f8a7fc03b6",
          "asset_sha256": "e1476bfb6197005033465cb2918b58c4eef024c336fcfcd11d9982fefdae8b53"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s02-c1-a2e87fe9bfb1",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A viewer sends an H T T P S request to CloudFront. The distribution is the public entry point; the S three bucket does not have to be public.",
          "text_sha256": "a2e87fe9bfb19f743c14d6ae11292645671af236501508964c8e4f44591fdab9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "df7e7e024710cde78bc4b3cb8cf1893aac021aca886ba831eb8f9806863a8c13",
          "asset_sha256": "fbd9545d625ce048173ca4301793d32009cfe8418ac1d43e827c81bfe993f27e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s02-c2-0283e66c1959",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If CloudFront needs to fetch the object, Origin Access Control lets it authenticate that origin request.",
          "text_sha256": "0283e66c19596e1dd804026badda51d83b9b9e805f39e8abbc06a9c30d7f1652",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0283e66c19596e1dd804026badda51d83b9b9e805f39e8abbc06a9c30d7f1652",
          "asset_sha256": "fbd9545d625ce048173ca4301793d32009cfe8418ac1d43e827c81bfe993f27e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s02-c3-7076dd590929",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The bucket policy grants the distribution access. Use a regular S three bucket origin for O A C, not its website endpoint.",
          "text_sha256": "7076dd59092929242481b4823d44ddade5c188a4175fc21dbf8f4ee68832002d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7ce71165576967827f2c77f0d43e9f5a5a21722789b910e41c92084ead9b5638",
          "asset_sha256": "fbd9545d625ce048173ca4301793d32009cfe8418ac1d43e827c81bfe993f27e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s02-c4-92fbbcee7ea3",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Store the static images, C S S and scripts as objects in S three.",
          "text_sha256": "92fbbcee7ea3c5a30cd43fa4a2e246ff4bac1c8b70ebd4db3563ba2e911e6410",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0fec15105c89db5c6e7ff76322fcfd04f137d3681be2b6174ea60052ca007e81",
          "asset_sha256": "fbd9545d625ce048173ca4301793d32009cfe8418ac1d43e827c81bfe993f27e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s02-c5-07c3fcfcaddf",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "CloudFront can return a cached copy from the edge without asking S three for it on every request.",
          "text_sha256": "07c3fcfcaddfe86e3fb82d737d4f42e9bc53e98a3c926408c24d8ee2bf956828",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0e7ec5facf2b4d3c2152233e6d40efa49eab86688ff850b8547b36922cd8f1e1",
          "asset_sha256": "fbd9545d625ce048173ca4301793d32009cfe8418ac1d43e827c81bfe993f27e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s02-c6-77febd4d6005",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Keep dynamic application logic in a separate compute service. Delivering a file does not make S three a compute runtime.",
          "text_sha256": "77febd4d6005b7ce533d49cfcd2eca3afcdc4b65f8c6b00a9a069ce6099a8318",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ebe4ba84979508188fce5122748f86d0d14c050fb0fc78ccf273ca27f58e63c9",
          "asset_sha256": "fbd9545d625ce048173ca4301793d32009cfe8418ac1d43e827c81bfe993f27e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s03-c1-91fa3cabb76a",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Choose Standard for frequently accessed data when you also want storage across Availability Zones. It has no minimum storage duration. The latency by itself does not distinguish these three classes.",
          "text_sha256": "91fa3cabb76af40cf458c16b3b4b11982de8dce0be7ad7d48b5e462ed908c303",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "91fa3cabb76af40cf458c16b3b4b11982de8dce0be7ad7d48b5e462ed908c303",
          "asset_sha256": "d35c7ca12252eafabbc3d5d8438395209881d5c9141b5572356db9c64df45796"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s03-c2-315dbb707477",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Standard Infrequent Access still spans zones and returns data in milliseconds, but adds retrieval charges plus minimum duration and billable-size considerations. A file read often or deleted quickly can cost more than expected.",
          "text_sha256": "315dbb707477b7888356892b732313242d8738ed187bfa6afb47bf8604cedd4d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "315dbb707477b7888356892b732313242d8738ed187bfa6afb47bf8604cedd4d",
          "asset_sha256": "d35c7ca12252eafabbc3d5d8438395209881d5c9141b5572356db9c64df45796"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p03-redo-s03-c3-4ec37868c55b",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "One Zone Infrequent Access keeps the data in one Availability Zone. Use it only when a separate copy or recreation can cover that zone's loss. Price is not a substitute for the recovery requirement.",
          "text_sha256": "4ec37868c55b1c9d497d3fbd1cec04fd8ff3f310d17e32f4a0d404460edc71f0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4ec37868c55b1c9d497d3fbd1cec04fd8ff3f310d17e32f4a0d404460edc71f0",
          "asset_sha256": "d35c7ca12252eafabbc3d5d8438395209881d5c9141b5572356db9c64df45796"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "04",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p04-visual-walkthrough-v3",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e",
        "2": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5",
        "3": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s01-c1-802d4869f9cb",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose the archive class by how quickly an application must read the data. Glacier Instant Retrieval offers millisecond access without a restore request, but has retrieval charges and a ninety-day minimum duration.",
          "text_sha256": "802d4869f9cb6311958923108e5d895a9213762840816c0707a8098636d123f0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "802d4869f9cb6311958923108e5d895a9213762840816c0707a8098636d123f0",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s01-c2-d16741fc70b5",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Flexible Retrieval needs a restore before the application can read the archived object. Retrieval choices trade speed and cost. Confirm that the recovery window includes waiting for the restore to finish.",
          "text_sha256": "d16741fc70b5ae3ac227e0fb9dd57b80dc50c97be2897cdbf5a514d004650a9a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "d16741fc70b5ae3ac227e0fb9dd57b80dc50c97be2897cdbf5a514d004650a9a",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s01-c3-a4f12f603e10",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Deep Archive targets longer retention with generally longer retrieval lead time and a one-hundred-eighty-day minimum storage duration. Use it only when that recovery delay is acceptable; a cheap archive that misses the deadline does not meet the requirement.",
          "text_sha256": "a4f12f603e108b966453e59db1b684594d51ec11cc913376202f130be282ab6b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a4f12f603e108b966453e59db1b684594d51ec11cc913376202f130be282ab6b",
          "asset_sha256": "cba464fab65d2f69eda48c02c99e829e62113fac4d01d09215064d295d01941e"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s02-c1-5ee9aa2419cd",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Eligible objects start in Frequent Access. After thirty days without an access they can move to Infrequent Access, and after ninety to Archive Instant Access. Those automatic tiers do not require a restore before reading.",
          "text_sha256": "5ee9aa2419cd3fda05f933d1c46aceda6a6e70dce00e9526b62318673531c632",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "5ee9aa2419cd3fda05f933d1c46aceda6a6e70dce00e9526b62318673531c632",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s02-c2-643e52f3cb33",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Optional Archive Access can start at ninety days without access, and the object needs a restore before it can be read. That is different from automatic Archive Instant Access.",
          "text_sha256": "643e52f3cb3346514df4e8983f3e7a9d00ecb62bbdd6deb862b85595db04e469",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "643e52f3cb3346514df4e8983f3e7a9d00ecb62bbdd6deb862b85595db04e469",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s02-c3-c14241935cc6",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Optional Deep Archive Access starts no earlier than one hundred eighty days without access. It also needs a restore before reading.",
          "text_sha256": "c14241935cc60beff04bcb1b645c4254588301a6cdebeb48f780aa0e7298783f",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c14241935cc60beff04bcb1b645c4254588301a6cdebeb48f780aa0e7298783f",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s02-c4-77ac8492fa5a",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Objects under one hundred twenty-eight kilobytes stay in Frequent Access and are not monitored for tiering. Eligible objects can incur a monitoring and automation charge, so consider the size mix.",
          "text_sha256": "77ac8492fa5ad25315f45e18ee3cf1c08c802b12c1784a4ef6729ef5e031dc8c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "77ac8492fa5ad25315f45e18ee3cf1c08c802b12c1784a4ef6729ef5e031dc8c",
          "asset_sha256": "e9212162838fe4ac6f9552e9cc40625045b60bd8ae41946b5affdefb86744fb5"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s03-c1-cd990bd020ba",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The current object version has its own supported transition or expiration action. In a versioned bucket, expiring a current version can make a delete marker current; that does not automatically remove the older data.",
          "text_sha256": "cd990bd020bafbe6bcecb6b755e07f1f3208880fef305b86d979674799403ae4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "cd990bd020bafbe6bcecb6b755e07f1f3208880fef305b86d979674799403ae4",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s03-c2-f76c9efda0bb",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Older versions need separate noncurrent transition or expiration rules. Before removing them, check the recovery window, minimum-duration charges and storage-class constraints.",
          "text_sha256": "f76c9efda0bbbc8e7f4c85e47227343a920cf5f4bd29fadb0dc8805360c049e9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f76c9efda0bbbc8e7f4c85e47227343a920cf5f4bd29fadb0dc8805360c049e9",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p04-redo-s03-c3-0d608d1afce3",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Expired delete markers can be cleaned up only when eligible. A prefix or tag filter limits the objects in scope and does not name a physical folder. Verify the policy against a sample key and all its versions before relying on it.",
          "text_sha256": "0d608d1afce3740aa923d7c53250cf4476cad5db24b853f56e180e1df8b14837",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0d608d1afce3740aa923d7c53250cf4476cad5db24b853f56e180e1df8b14837",
          "asset_sha256": "e908dcd44019e92ed3af3ade73c42512cd250115958243ef993d1075617a6fc2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "05",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p05-visual-walkthrough-v3",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322",
        "2": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830",
        "3": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s01-c1-4574e5ca15b1",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Learn to choose a replication destination and tell which objects will actually arrive. Start with the versioned source bucket.",
          "text_sha256": "4574e5ca15b1daa6593c1b81c6bd9d7821fbe914722ed9e2d3b2286a85575776",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4574e5ca15b1daa6593c1b81c6bd9d7821fbe914722ed9e2d3b2286a85575776",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s01-c2-18e094bfe2f3",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose Same-Region Replication when copies must stay in the same Region. Both example buckets here are in US East one.",
          "text_sha256": "18e094bfe2f334288515ffbd970f1a2c06491ebee2d81cb66060755cef342d1e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "18e094bfe2f334288515ffbd970f1a2c06491ebee2d81cb66060755cef342d1e",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s01-c3-81a562ee59f8",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Choose Cross-Region Replication when the recovery requirement calls for another Region. Here the destination is US West two.",
          "text_sha256": "81a562ee59f89909c5ac2998da2d0be5e092b11928c236d22e5323a437a964a2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "81a562ee59f89909c5ac2998da2d0be5e092b11928c236d22e5323a437a964a2",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s01-c4-f4d853682b8f",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Enable versioning on both buckets so the rule can copy eligible object versions.",
          "text_sha256": "f4d853682b8f054553d85ac1943d669ffafe2d468a15cd19ce47310d5056e5c9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f4d853682b8f054553d85ac1943d669ffafe2d468a15cd19ce47310d5056e5c9",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s01-c5-b5bdd4f328a7",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Configure the replication rule and its I A M role. Do not assume the bucket configuration itself is replicated.",
          "text_sha256": "b5bdd4f328a756df3ba6de43a3e3976f0bbf7b5e5015e80288d923affb4fbfc9",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "fc841cce524c739f1818acc8e22f441e3609413ee3e22d383962c068b35c1cf2",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s01-c6-8b6ba32e124c",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "For S S E K M S objects, configure supported encryption settings and key permissions. Test an eligible encrypted version at the destination.",
          "text_sha256": "8b6ba32e124c03499f09414aa9936a7ec56d5a4131c9bd5729032a89dbc1101d",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "0390735fe40f3bf3ea3516d920e7bab3f9b2200fc0ab6b876d1e4a1d673b84fc",
          "asset_sha256": "a0e9e6fa69d8064da2aa1432f41b49fa367cccaa6fe8bebbf18262867ce4c322"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s02-c1-07a5038f1ffd",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "New eligible objects written after the rule is configured follow the live replication path. Use monitoring and, if the live timing requirement calls for it, evaluate S three Replication Time Control. A rule alone does not prove a specific object has arrived.",
          "text_sha256": "07a5038f1ffd67425811c6b2e5cf308bed7340557b94b7103351f20e3a97c1ac",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9f14f657853c4317f8f27363af80c2f7747fc2b37448f8e007047367c977ac9d",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s02-c2-2c609c96dcf7",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Objects that predate the rule are not automatically backfilled. S three Batch Replication can handle eligible existing objects or repair gaps, but Replication Time Control does not apply to Batch Replication.",
          "text_sha256": "2c609c96dcf75fae7e756f4f94ccf55a03ea353161aae9f020436832e70265df",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c60150a6409116552df39d49c0210cd8e30ee2de8b7a360b4f49db2415b97324",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s02-c3-a6dd2d3dccee",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Replicate delete markers only when your rule supports and enables it. Deleting a particular version at the source does not perform the same delete at the destination. Test the exact behavior against the recovery policy.",
          "text_sha256": "a6dd2d3dcceed9ed7b7306cba4909487a57d943b5523adbd5858e753508d0638",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a6dd2d3dcceed9ed7b7306cba4909487a57d943b5523adbd5858e753508d0638",
          "asset_sha256": "ca4a2eee9d0f4901b16bcb15ad9fa894cf4837a7b62e399ade34fd2165afb830"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s03-c1-33e67b7ec3bc",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Start from the event the application needs, such as an object creation, removal or restore. A notification lets a consumer react without the uploader having to run the downstream job itself.",
          "text_sha256": "33e67b7ec3bc6c392ff69a22d5b4f57097f301f12c332886249aa937f445f0b0",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "33e67b7ec3bc6c392ff69a22d5b4f57097f301f12c332886249aa937f445f0b0",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s03-c2-a0803f74d942",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "Use supported key filters, for example an invoices prefix and a dot CSV suffix, to narrow what invokes the consumer. Do not treat the prefix or suffix as an arbitrary wildcard. Also keep derived output outside the trigger scope where needed.",
          "text_sha256": "a0803f74d942f1a1883176bc020fda18eac7ed32ad99e47a5f7ef4b96b3f38f8",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a0803f74d942f1a1883176bc020fda18eac7ed32ad99e47a5f7ef4b96b3f38f8",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p05-redo-s03-c3-77e8e656f0c9",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The direct destinations shown are Lambda, a standard S Q S queue or a standard S N S topic. Grant delivery permission, then verify receipt. Events can repeat or arrive out of order, so make processing idempotent instead of assuming an exactly-once transaction.",
          "text_sha256": "77e8e656f0c9fac00bad6fd58472217fc79825406be854609e2601cfecbf818e",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "7f676d27eac27262f9b8a5ef600ed31b1b98743715d33be8bff344aa580cc625",
          "asset_sha256": "b42b1bc561b63e3ea58dcae5c1bd7762eb822f3c18212e63f62618066ee0891f"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
